From bf99ce199b8529e5e2d6c449316935e64c004bb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kugguk2022 <kugguk2022@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:06:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repurpose toward a distributed-inference, coverage-focused
 research framework

Adds lotteries_core: a common InferenceProvider protocol, reproducible
provenance-carrying envelopes, an honest pari-mutuel ROI layer (unpopularity
lever + instant-game remaining-prize EV), coverage/diversity metrics, and a
deterministic diversity-aware equal-budget aggregator ("coordinated distributed
inference"). Wraps frequency baseline + unpopularity + a GLM/XGBoost/deep-MLP
popularity ensemble (soft deps). Adds a forward-only equal-budget benchmark CLI.

Fixes the legacy POI for forecasting via an opt-in causal variant (no look-ahead,
justified time baseline instead of Euler-phi) without changing behaviour the
branch strategies depend on.

Adds scope/ethics + geography docs and a README scope banner making the product
boundary explicit: negative-sum game, no draw prediction, no pooled funds, no
ticket purchase, simulation-only, no guaranteed-winnings claim.

Includes tests (protocol, envelope reproducibility, deterministic aggregation,
honest ROI direction, causal POI, benchmark determinism) and community/tooling
files (pre-commit, CoC, SECURITY, issue/PR templates, CHANGELOG).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
